=== :cwindow with no errors opens no window
ref:    quickfix.txt *:cwindow*
quote:  "Open the quickfix window when there are recognized errors."
given:
  o|ne
  two
keys:   :file x.txt<CR>:cwindow<CR>
expect:
  o|ne
  two
win:    1/1

=== :cwindow with errors opens the quickfix window
ref:    quickfix.txt *:cwindow*
quote:  "Open the quickfix window when there are recognized errors."
given:
  o|ne
  two
  three
  four
keys:   :file x.txt<CR>:cexpr ["x.txt:2:3:first", "x.txt:4:1:second"]<CR>:cwindow<CR>
# the quickfix window
expect:
  |x.txt\|2 col 3\| first
  x.txt\|4 col 1\| second
win:    2/2

=== :cdo runs a command at every entry
ref:    quickfix.txt *:cdo*
quote:  "Execute {cmd} in each valid entry in the quickfix list."
given:
  o|ne
  two
  three
  four
keys:   :file x.txt<CR>:cexpr ["x.txt:1:1:a", "x.txt:2:1:b", "x.txt:4:1:c"]<CR>:cdo s/$/!/<CR>
expect:
  one!
  two!
  three
  |four!
msg:    (3 of 3): c

=== :vimgrep searches a buffer that has a name and jumps to the first match
ref:    quickfix.txt *:vimgrep*
quote:  "Search for {pattern} in the files {file} ... and set the error list to the matches."
given:
  o|ne
  two
  three
  four
  five
keys:   :file x.txt<CR>:vimgrep /o/ %<CR>
expect:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
  five
msg:    (1 of 3): one

=== :cnext after :vimgrep goes to the next match's column
ref:    quickfix.txt *:vimgrep*
quote:  "Search for {pattern} in the files {file} ... and set the error list to the matches."
given:
  o|ne
  two
  three
  four
  five
keys:   :file x.txt<CR>:vimgrep /e$/ %<CR>:cnext<CR>
expect:
  one
  two
  thre|e
  four
  five
msg:    (2 of 3): three

=== :vimgrep adds each line once without g
ref:    quickfix.txt *:vimgrep*
quote:  "Without the 'g' flag each line is added only once."
given:
  o|ne
  two
  three
  four
  five
keys:   :file x.txt<CR>:vimgrep /e/ %<CR>:clast<CR>
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  four
  fiv|e
msg:    (3 of 3): five

=== :vimgrep with g adds every match
ref:    quickfix.txt *:vimgrep*
quote:  "With 'g' every match is added."
given:
  o|ne
  two
  three
  four
  five
keys:   :file x.txt<CR>:vimgrep /e/g %<CR>:cc 3<CR>
# the second match in "three"
expect:
  one
  two
  thre|e
  four
  five
msg:    (3 of 4): three

=== :vimgrep with j only fills the list
ref:    quickfix.txt *:vimgrep*
quote:  "With 'j' only the quickfix list is updated."
given:
  o|ne
  two
  three
keys:   :file x.txt<CR>:vimgrep /e$/j %<CR>
expect:
  o|ne
  two
  three
jumps:

=== :vimgrep with no match
ref:    quickfix.txt *:vimgrep*
quote:  "Search for {pattern} in the files {file} ... and set the error list to the matches."
given:
  o|ne
  two
keys:   :file x.txt<CR>:vimgrep /zzz/ %<CR>
expect:
  o|ne
  two
msg:    E480: No match: zzz

=== :vimgrep takes a pattern without slashes
ref:    quickfix.txt *:vimgrep*
quote:  "Like above, but instead of enclosing the pattern in a non-ID character use a white space separated pattern."
given:
  o|ne
  two
  three
  four
  five
keys:   :file x.txt<CR>:vimgrep o %<CR>:cnext<CR>
expect:
  one
  tw|o
  three
  four
  five
msg:    (2 of 3): two
